.TH gitaway-profile-set 1  "gitaway 0.0.0" "gitaway manual"
.SH NAME
gitaway\-profile\-set \- Change one setting, keeping the file\*(Aqs comments and layout
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgitaway profile set\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fINAME\fR> <\fIKEY\fR> <\fIVALUE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change one setting, keeping the file\*(Aqs comments and layout.
.PP
Keys are dotted paths, such as `home.ssh` or `transport.wireguard.mtu`. Quote parts that contain dots: `\*(Aqhosts."192.0.2.10"\*(Aq`. The change is checked before it\*(Aqs saved.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
The profile to change
.TP
<\fIKEY\fR>
The setting, as a dotted path
.TP
<\fIVALUE\fR>
The new value. Numbers and `true`/`false` are read as such; anything else is a string
